    "created_at": "2015-09-30T07:22:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-30T19:01:17Z",
    "body": "- [x] img width height\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3642\n  - Everyone supports \"0\"\n  - Gecko turns \"0.9%\" to \"0%\", WebKit/Blink/IE11 don't\n- [x] table width height\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3644\n  - \"0\" and \"0%\" should be ignored\n  - Gecko/IE11 ignore \"0.1\" and \"0.1%\"\n  - WebKit/Blink ignore width:0 in CSS\n- [x] col width\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3645\n  - IE11 ignores \"0\", \"0.1\", \"0.1%\"\n  - Gecko applies \"0\" but ignores \"0%\" and \"0.1%\"\n  - Blink/WebKit ignore small values (in the above, < 6px)\n- [x] tr height\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3647\n  - Gecko applies height=1 and height=1% and style=height:0.9% but ignores 0, 0%, style=height:0, 0.9, 0.9%\n  - WebKit/Blink apply all\n  - IE11 applies 1, 1%, style=height:0, style=height=0.9%; ignores 0, 0%, 0.9, 0.9%\n- [x] th/td width\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3648\n  - Gecko/IE11 apply 1, style=width:0, 1%; ignores 0, 0%, style=width:0%, 0.9, 0.9%\n  - WebKit/Blink apply 1, 1%; ignores the others\n- [x] th/td height\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3649\n  - Gecko applies 1, style=height:0, 1%, ignores 0, 0%, style=height:0%, 0.9, 0.9%\n  - WebKit/Blink apply 1, 1%, ignore the others\n  - IE11 applies 1, style=height:0, style=height:0%, 1%; ignores the others\n- [x] hr width\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3650\n  - Gecko/WebKit/Blink apply all, but 0.9% is interpreted as 0\n  - IE11 applies all; 0.9% is properly supported\n- [x] applet, embed, iframe, img, object, input[type=image], marquee vspace hspace (check 0.9%)\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3651 embed vspace\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3653 img vspace\n  - 0 is the default, so there is no difference between applying and not applying 0 AFAICT\n  - Blink/WebKit support 0.9 and 0.9%. Percentages for vspace refer to the width of the containing block (like the spec, since it maps to margin-top).\n  - Gecko ignores 0.9 and 0.9%. Percentages for vspace refer to the _height_ of the containing block.\n  - IE11 is like Gecko, but doesn't support vspace for embed\n- [x] applet, embed, iframe, object, video, input[type=image], marquee width height\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3654 iframe width\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3655 video width\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3656 marquee width\n  - like img\n- [x] <blockquote>In quirks mode, a td element or a th element that has a nowrap attribute but also has a width attribute whose value, when parsed using the rules for parsing dimension values, is found to be a length (not an error or a number classified as a percentage), is expected to have a presentational hint setting the element's 'white-space' property to 'normal', overriding the rule in the CSS block above that sets it to 'nowrap'.</blockquote>\n  - http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3657\n  - IE11/Gecko/WebKit/Blink don't reset white-space for width=0.\n  - WebKit/Blink have this quirk in standards mode, too.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
