    "created_at": "2015-10-01T11:17:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-01T11:17:35Z",
    "body": "http://webdevdata.org/ data set 2015-01-08 (780 Mb) 87,000 pages.\n\n```\n$ find . -type f -print0 | xargs -0 -P 4 -n 40 grep -iEo \"<(td|th|col|table|tr)\\s([^>]+\\s)?(width|height)=[\\\"']?0%?[\\\"']?(\\s|>)\" > ../width-height-0.txt\n```\n\nI inspected the matches in Nightly and applied `width:0` or `height:0` as appropriate in devtools to see if the rendered result was affected. 20 first URLs were unaffected (some had changed), then I found one that regressed its rendering:\n\nhttp://magiran.com/\n\ncurrent rendering:\n<img width=\"995\" alt=\"screen shot 2015-10-01 at 13 12 50\" src=\"https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/244772/10219295/0bca83b4-683e-11e5-897d-a3222b9c6905.png\">\n\nstyle=\"width:0\"\n<img width=\"995\" alt=\"screen shot 2015-10-01 at 13 13 12\" src=\"https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/244772/10219296/0bcd7d62-683e-11e5-8f9c-2730983374b2.png\">\n\nSo I suppose we should keep ignoring 0 and 0% for the table-related elements...\n",
